Round 1, read as laid out (6 and 12 PDF pages) by three fictional readers, test instruments: a conference team member with their own agent, a newsroom builder, a first-build finisher. All three got the factory in both editions; all three would start tomorrow from the 3-page edition, only "maybe" from the 10-page one (yes from its draft): the action page comes late and the pages before it read unfinished.

Yours, page by page:
1. Page 2 (03, 10): the contents is ten bare titles without page numbers on an empty sheet, the worst page for all three; page numbers and a line each, or fold it into the cover so the story starts on the second sheet.
2. Page 12 (10): "Where this came from" prints repository paths in mixed serif and monospace; plain source names in one typeface, the paths online (two of three).
3. The cast bar and the boxes: about a point larger for a phone (the conference team member).
Not a finding: the running header the readers saw was my own stamp on the copies I built; yours has none.

